 LRU Cache:(Least Recently Used Cache)
 Its a cache replacement policy that removes the least recently used
 item when the cache becomes full.
 
 
 
 Cache - temporary memory area it frequently used data.
 
 
 Cache capacity=3
 
 Operation     cache
 put 1         [1]
 put 2         [2,1]
 put 3         [3,2,1]
 
 get 1         [1,3,2]  
 
 put 4         [1,3,4]
 
 Brute force: ArrayList  - put - O(n), get - O(n), evict - O(1) 
 
 Efficient solution: Hashmap & doubly linked list
 
 search - O(1) - lookup
 insert/update/delete - O(1)
 
 MRU-----LRU
 
 head<-->nodes.....<-->tail
 
 
 Hashing: It is the process of converting data(key) into fixed size
 value using hash function.
 
 
 key ->  hash function -> hash code/value/ digest
 
 Why hashing used?
 i)Very fast searching
 ii)Fast data insertion/deletion
 iii)Efficient data storage
 
 hash()
 
 
 h(k)=k mod m   [k=key, m=table size]
 
 
 10 % 20= 10
 
 Hash collision: It occurs when two different keys produce the same
 hash code.(same index in the hash table)
 
 15  - 15%10 -> 5
 
 25  - 25%10 -> 5  25+1%10->6
 
 35  - 35%10 -> 5 
 
 Solution:
 
 i)Open addressing (Linear probing, Quadratic probing, double hashing )
 Instead of storing multiple elements in a linked list , find another
 empty location.
   
   Linear probing : Next Index=(currentIndex+i)%size; i=1,2,3... - high clustering
   Quadratic probing: : Next Index=(currentIndex+i*i)%size;      - mid clustering
   double hashing: Index=(hash1(key)+i x hash2(key)) % size      - low clustering
   
 ii)Separate chaining: Each bucket stores a linked list of elements.
 
 
 Clustering: 
 
 ['A' next] -->['B',next]-->['C',null]
 
 HashTable
 HashMap
 HashSet
 
 
 Problem 1: Given an array of strings, group the anagrams together.
 
 ["eat","tea","tan","ate","nat","bat"]
 
 [[eat,tea,ate],
  [tan,nat],
  [bat]
 ]
 
 
 Approach:
 1.Create a hashmap
 2.sort each word
 3.use sorted word as keys
 4.Store original word in the corresponding list.
 5.Return all groups 
 
 
 Two sum:
 Given an array and target value, return indices of two numbers
 whose sum equals target.
 
 arr=[2,7,11,15]
 target=9
 
 [0,1]
 
 
 target=13
 
 [0,2]
 
 Sub array sum equals K:
 Given an integer array nums and an integer k, return the total number
 of continuous subarrays whose sum equals k.
 
 nums =[1,1,1]
 taget=2
 
